---
import BaseLayout from "../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Incidetective | Michael"
  description="A backend incident investigation project built with TypeScript."
>
  <article class="project-detail">
    <header class="project-detail-header">
      <a href="/projects/" class="back-link">
        ← Back to projects
      </a>

      <p class="eyebrow">PERSONAL PROJECT · IN DEVELOPMENT</p>

      <h1>Incidetective</h1>

      <p class="project-lead">
        Exploring how backend engineers can investigate service incidents by
        organizing logs, evidence, and findings.
      </p>

      <div class="project-detail-links">
        <a
          href="https://github.com/Ohshi60/Incidetective"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
        >
          View source on GitHub ↗
        </a>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="project-detail-body">
      <section>
        <h2>The problem</h2>
        <p>
          Investigating service failures often means working through logs,
          identifying relevant events, and collecting evidence before
          understanding what went wrong.
        </p>
        <p>
          Incidetective is a learning project focused on making that
          investigation process more structured.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Technical approach</h2>
        <p>
          The project uses TypeScript and Node.js, with an emphasis on
          separating incident data, log evidence, and investigation logic.
        </p>
        <p>
          Automated tests help verify the expected behavior, including keeping
          evidence associated with the correct incident.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Project goals</h2>
        <p>
          The longer-term goal is to support searching synthetic logs,
          assembling investigation reports, and experimenting with optional
          AI-assisted analysis.
        </p>
        <p>
          The project is still in development, so these goals should not be
          interpreted as completed features.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Technologies</h2>
        <ul class="project-detail-tech">
          <li>TypeScript</li>
          <li>Node.js</li>
          <li>Vitest</li>
        </ul>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
